{"author":{"id":"1d5f412cdeafe9987ad9876b0995bf5032718543d34c038a50cdb41808e9874c"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788305117,"nonce":"obg4Ix7MQqlL0cOEULEfTab2GOI=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOULVc1M8AAAABPPhbag","github-url":"https://github.com/kanya-approve/torram-ng/issues/1","origin":"github"},"title":"Merged output is written at wrong offsets (silent corruption)","message":"`construct_file()` computes write positions as `file_info.start_offset + chunk_idx * piece_length`.\n\nTwo independent errors make this wrong:\n\n1. `chunk_idx` indexes only the pieces belonging to *this* torrent file (`fi.chunks` is built solely from pieces where `idx == file_idx`), but files rarely begin on a piece boundary. So `chunk_idx * piece_length` is not the byte offset of that piece within the file.\n2. `start_offset` is itself garbage — see the companion issue about `if not file_info.start_offset`.\n\nThe result is that correct, hash-verified piece data is written to incorrect locations in the output file. The merge path (`M`) therefore produces a corrupt file while reporting success.\n\nNothing re-hashes the result afterwards, so the corruption is silent.\n\nThis is the most serious defect in the tool.","files":null}]}